      "summary": "<img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/af/a0/afa04ee3-414f-4481-8d23-7e7c146f192e/content/images/2026/07/vuln_roundup.jpg\" alt=\"WolfSSL, GeoVision, VTK vulnerabilities\"><p>Cisco Talos&#x2019; Vulnerability Discovery &amp; Research team recently disclosed three vulnerabilities in WolfSSF, fourteen in GeoVision, and one vulnerability in VTK-DICOM.</p><p>The vulnerabilities mentioned in this blog post have been patched by their respective vendors, in adherence to<a href=\"https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/resources/vendor_vulnerability_policy.html\"><u> Cisco&#x2019;s third-party vulnerability disclosure policy</u></a>.&#xA0;</p><p>For Snort coverage that can detect the exploitation of these vulnerabilities, download the latest rule sets from<a href=\"https://snort.org/\"><u> Snort.org</u></a>, and our latest Vulnerability Advisories are always posted on<a href=\"https://talosintelligence.com/vulnerability_reports\"><u> Talos Intelligence&#x2019;s website</u></a>.</p><h2 id=\"wolfssl",
      "sourceUrl": "https://blog.talosintelligence.com/wolfssl-vulnerabilities/",
